<title>SINGAPORE: Lum Chang 1996 net profit up 47 pct.</title>
<headline>Lum Chang 1996 net profit up 47 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full year ended June 30 1996</p>
<p>(in million of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		   20.42   vs   13.91</p>
<p>    Group shares (cents)	6.30   vs    4.30</p>
<p>    Turnover		    260.71   vs  245.14</p>
<p>    Interest income	     3.77   vs    3.51</p>
<p>    Operating profit	   24.75   vs   20.74</p>
<p>    Associates		    5.63   vs    1.82</p>
<p>    Pretax			 30.39   vs   22.56</p>
<p>    Tax			    10.11   vs    8.92</p>
<p>    Minority			0.15   vs    0.28</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries	    25.61   vs   (0.96)</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)	    1.00   vs    1.00</p>
<p>Note- Construction based Lum Chang Holdings Ltd said the extraordinary item was mainly a realisation of a revaluation surplus of hotel interests. - Singapore Newsroom 65-8703080</p>
</text>
